Primer design helper program with support for multiple designs in one run.

Settings: Same for every design in a run - ref. genome, output directory, primer3 global tags
Job: One design request - coordinates, fusion or not, primer positions, rev-comp, name...
Result: The output for one job - parsed primer pairs (+ explain string), or error.

jobs = build_jobs(args)
results = [run_job(job, settings) for job in jobs]
write_outputs(results, settings)




Implementing RC-PCR design.

Add parameters for RC-PCR (see below)
Add ability for bulk primer design, i.e from a list of input coordinates

Key RC-PCR parameters/design process:

In short I pick them by eye, keeping them as short as possible.
I BLAT the sequence prior to design to look for regions of homology.
When designing, where possible I keep the length between 18-25bp, that the final 4 bases are not self-complimentary
(eg CATG)  and check that they have a Tm of circa 60C using:
 https://tmcalculator.neb.com/#!/main

 And SNP check binding sequences using:
https://genetools.org/SNPCheck/snpcheck.htm


the regions of interest for this project will be defined and so the locations where we can place the primers will be heavily constrained by this.

Picking the target specific sequences is the time consuming bit – unless you can get AI to do it for a large number of targets.

Once we have these sequences converting them to RC probes is straight forward – essentially append a tag sequence ta each of the target specific sequencing and reverse compliment the whole lot.
